==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|dayumn}}

===Etymology===
[[respelling|Respelling]] of {{m|en|damn}} to reflect [[emphatic]] stress and a Southern US [[drawl]], in which the vowel is broken into gliding vowels.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|[ˈdæ̙jəm]|[ˈdeəjəm]}}

===Interjection===
{{en-interj|head=dayum!}}

# {{lb|en|slang|emphatic}} {{pronunciation spelling of|en|damn|from=Southern US}}
#: ''Oh, did you ''see'' her?! '''Dayum!''' She was looking good!"